  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Propel Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  PROPEL Youth and Gender uses policy, advocacy, governance, and financing approaches to strengthen the enabling environment and to specifically address the needs of youth and adolescents. The project addresses gender equity and equality, and the intersection of youth and gender. This fiscal year, PROPEL Youth and Gender will support country governments to leverage the Green Climate Fund financing to support gender transformative, youth responsive FP/RH programming. The project will also work with local partners in urban settings to strengthen the capacity of local organizations, including youth-led organizations and governments, to implement social accountability approaches. PROPEL Youth and Gender will also support Missions and country governments in addressing female genital mutilation/cutting and child, early and force marriage activities based on the priorities of the Mission(s) and country context.</narrative>
  </description>
